@spec/language.sigil import { SigilLanguage, SigilModuleIndex }
@integrations/skills/sigil/design-compilation-review.sigil import { SigilDesignCompilationReview }

component SigilAuthoringWorkflow {
  goal {
    Author coherent Sigil boundaries, Facets, Tag identities, imports,
    summary sources, and durable *decision rationale* as an initial
    *written draft*, then revise it from provisional design evidence.
  }

  interface {
ImportSemanticsGuidance {
      ImportSemanticsGuidance adapts ImportSemantics into authoring guidance.

      inspects the complete accessible *imported Tag scope* before creating a
      local component or Concept with overlapping meaning

      reuses every semantically matching imported component, and every Tag
      introduced in `interface`, so dependency contracts retain
      *provider identity* and vocabulary
    }

ModuleIndexFileGuidance {
      ModuleIndexFileGuidance adapts ModuleIndexFile into authoring guidance.

      keeps one small local *summary component* and assembles an intentional
      directory-import surface from cohesive imported components

      retains only boundary-wide goal, interface, architectural constraints, and
      durable design decisions

      delegates independently owned state, operational logic, lifecycle, and
      implementation detail to components and expands colocated with their owners
    }

ConceptWorkflow {
      discovers reusable identities across the complete component, matching expands,
      accessible imports, and relevant direct consumers

      proactively recommends Concept names for recurring cross-contract concerns
      and each useful *public identity*, with concrete guidance for leaving
      Facets ungrouped

      checks deterministic *Tag diagnostics* before proposing names

      uses one proposal-only Concept-name subagent when subagents are available
    }

FacetDisciplineGuidance {
      FacetDisciplineGuidance adapts FacetDiscipline into authoring
      guidance.

      preserves one distinct idea per blank-line-delimited Facet and allows
      physical prose wrapping without changing *semantic identity*

      places an attached EmbeddedContent directly after its introducing prose
      without a blank line

      limits ordinary prose to 79 content characters without counting leading
      indentation
    }

DecisionRationaleWorkflow {
      records each material *selected choice* and the rationale needed for
      future review, maintenance, and agent sessions

      applies a consistent *authoring convention* while preserving the
      language's free-form decisions syntax

      uses automatically projected direct-dependency decisions as scoped rationale
      without treating them as imported public contract

      audits every new or changed material selected choice for durable rationale
      before written-Sigil design compilation can be accepted

      reports each choice as covered by a decisions occurrence or intentionally
      omitted with concrete evidence
    }
  }
}

expand SigilAuthoringWorkflow {
  logic {
DirectAuthoringLifecycle {
      After *material design intent* is resolved, write the exact scoped Sigil
      draft directly to the selected file before DesignCompilationReview.

      Use DesignCompilationReview evidence only to revise, validate, and
      complete that written draft. Investigate native *Disjoint findings* and
      preserve *Loose warnings*. Missing reconstruction does not prevent
      authoring.
    }

ImportSemantics {
      Inspect accessible imported components and Tags introduced in `interface`
      before proposing local identities.

      Reuse every semantic match and create a local identity only for a materially
      distinct responsibility or meaning.
    }

ModuleIndexFile {
      Extract independently changing responsibilities and material state, lifecycle,
      or operational logic into colocated components and expands.

      Import the components intended for directory shorthand and leave the local
      summary focused on boundary-wide architecture.
    }

ConceptWorkflow {
      Inspect meaning before choosing Tag identities. Use native
      DesignCompilationReview for available *semantic evidence*. Concept
      grouping does not depend on a removed evaluator stage or separate
      warning approval.

      Inspect the affected section, every other section of the component, and every
      matching expand for the same semantic idea.

      Inspect accessible imported Tags introduced in `interface` before creating
      a local identity.

      Inspect direct importers for relevant use cases and established terminology.

      Traverse transitive importers only when a Tag is re-exposed or Tag scope
      ambiguity must be assessed.

      Classify each affected region as remaining ungrouped, local reuse, imported
      public reuse, or a justified new identity.

      Prefer grouping when several contracts describe the same concern. Recurrence
      is a useful signal, not a minimum occurrence count for a public identity.

      Keep shared component-wide promises direct when clearer and express links
      between Concepts through the actual operations, conditions, and values.

      Give the proposal-only subagent the affected regions, complete component and
      expands, local occurrences, imported candidates, consumer evidence, and graph
      paths.

      After written grouping changes, return to DesignCompilationReview before
      glossary candidate extraction.
    }

DecisionRationaleWorkflow {
      Use one concise PascalCase Concept for each material decision.

      Record Decision and Scope for every authored material decision.

      Scope states the governed boundary and important exclusions without attempting
      to enumerate every current dependent.

      Record Assumptions, Trade-offs, Design issues addressed, Discarded
      alternatives, Consequences, and Revisit when when materially applicable.

      Omit an inapplicable rationale label instead of adding filler.

      Reuse an accessible Concept name when decisions concern the same semantic
      idea.

      Scope states the local boundary of a contextual decision occurrence; Tag
      reuse does not make a decision transitively binding.

      Keep the binding selected outcome in constraints and use decisions to explain
      why it was selected.

      Before presenting an exact *semantic proposal*, inventory every new or
      changed selected choice expressed across goal, interface, state, logic,
      constraints, and cases.

      Treat a choice as material when future review, maintenance, or implementation
      cannot safely reconstruct why it was selected or what alternatives it excludes.

      Map each material selected choice to a matching decisions occurrence that
      preserves its durable rationale.

      When the *binding outcome* is confirmed but its *decision record* is
      missing, include the exact decision record in the semantic proposal.

      When the governing rationale is unresolved or conflicts with evidence, return
      to DesignConversation in the applicable mode before proposing the decision
      record.

      Repeat the *decision-rationale coverage audit* after writing validated
      Sigil and before relying on the changed contract for implementation.
    }
  }

  constraints {
ImportSemantics {
      Tag reuse is maximized only where meaning is coherent; superficially
      similar but materially distinct Tags retain separate identities.

      Imported public identities are reused directly without aliases, dotted
      notation, local synonyms, or duplicated provider contracts.
    }

ModuleIndexFile {
      Every Facet in ModuleIndexFile applies to the indexed directory or
      configured boundary as a whole.

      Material operational logic, mutable state, detailed lifecycle behavior, and
      independently changing policy belong to their owning components or expands.

      ModuleIndexFile may retain only genuinely boundary-wide state or orchestration
      that cannot coherently belong to a narrower owner.

      Smallness is assessed by responsibility and ownership rather than an arbitrary
      line-count threshold.
    }

ConceptWorkflow {
      Actively identify the Concepts in a component and use Concept names to
      connect their Facets across contracts. Preserve ungrouped and mixed Facets;
      smaller components may need no additional Concept.

      Do not manufacture a Concept per function, Facet, or contract, require each
      Concept in all seven contracts, or group remaining prose under a catch-all Tag.

      Concept grouping does not dictate implementation decomposition or establish
      behavioral equality. Related Facets retain their contract roles and support.

      *Consumer terminology* is naming evidence but is not reusable identity unless
      accessible through valid imports.

      The subagent reports each region, grouping decision, new or reused status,
      occurrences, graph paths, rejected alternatives, and proposed concise names.

      Authorized Concept creation, reuse, regrouping, and renaming are written
      directly to scoped Sigil, then return to DesignCompilationReview.

      Concept-name work does not invoke anchor persistence, proposal, or
      reconciliation behavior.
    }

FacetDiscipline {
      Concepts group coherent identities without merging distinct semantic
      ideas into one unit.

      Goal and decisions references never satisfy *strict import use*.

      EmbeddedContent content remains excluded from import, Tag, glossary, and
      ownership reference evidence.
    }

    DecisionRationaleWorkflow {
      Decision records summarize durable rationale rather than prompts, raw session
      transcripts, or hidden reasoning.

      Responsibility, accountability, approver, and handoff metadata are outside the
      initial authoring convention.

      The absence of a decisions section is structurally valid but blocks skill
      semantic readiness when a material selected choice lacks durable rationale.

      A material selected choice cannot proceed to implementation review without
      decision-rationale coverage.

      A trivial, mechanically derived, or safely reconstructable choice does not
      require a filler decision record.

      Successful CLI validation does not establish decision-rationale coverage.
    }
  }

  decisions {
ImportSemantics {
      Decision: Maximize coherent reuse of accessible imported public identities
      before introducing local component or Tag identities.

      Scope: Governs Sigil authoring across direct imports and accessible public
      Tag scopes.

      Trade-offs: Authors must inspect provider contracts before choosing local
      names.

      Design issues addressed: Local synonyms and duplicated contracts fragment
      architecture vocabulary and obscure dependency ownership.

      Consequences: Importers remain consistent with *provider Tag* scopes
      while materially distinct meanings retain independent identities.
    }

ModuleIndexFile {
      Decision: Keep ModuleIndexFile as a small architectural summary and intentional
      directory-import assembly surface.

      Scope: Governs configured-boundary and internal module indexes; excludes
      independently owned operational behavior and state.

      Trade-offs: A modular boundary uses more Sigil files and explicit imports.

      Design issues addressed: Large module indexes encourage generated god modules
      whose unrelated responsibilities change together.

      Consequences: Detailed responsibilities move beside their owners while the
      index preserves the high-level architecture and public usable Tag vocabulary.

      Revisit when: A boundary-wide responsibility cannot be assigned coherently to a
      narrower component.
    }

DecisionRationaleWorkflow {
      Decision: Require a decision-rationale coverage audit before written-Sigil
      design compilation can be accepted and again after Sigil is written.

      Scope: Governs new or changed material selected choices in scoped semantic
      Sigil writes; excludes trivial, mechanically derived, and safely
      reconstructable choices.

      Trade-offs: Every material write requires an additional coverage review and may
      require more Facets.

      Design issues addressed: Material workflow choices previously advanced without
      coverage because decision authoring described record format but not its audit.

      Consequences: Missing rationale blocks accepted design evidence, and exact
      decision records must be included in the written Sigil.

      Revisit when: Deterministic tooling can identify decision-rationale coverage
      without treating model judgment as language validity.
    }

    TagProposalIsolation {
      Decision: Use one proposal-only Concept-name subagent when available and
      otherwise perform the same evidence-bounded analysis in the primary agent.

      Scope: Governs Tag reuse, grouping, and name proposals after accepted
      DesignCompilationReview evidence; excludes repository mutation and approval.

      Trade-offs: Delegation adds coordination overhead and may be unavailable.

      Design issues addressed: A separate proposal pass reduces anchoring on the
      primary author's preferred grouping without multiplying competing proposals.

      Discarded alternatives: Multiple parallel naming agents and subagent edit
      authority were rejected as noisy and outside this authoring workflow.

      Consequences: Exactly one advisory proposal is independently checked; the
      primary agent remains responsible for validation and user review.
    }
  }

  cases {
ImportSemantics {
      An importer reuses an accessible provider Tag instead of introducing a
      synonymous local Tag, but creates a new identity when the meanings differ.
    }

ModuleIndexFile {
      A boundary with multiple independently owned responsibilities declares their
      components beside their owners and imports the intended public components into
      ModuleIndexFile instead of placing operational detail in its local summary.
    }

ConceptWorkflow {
      The same idea in an interface and matching expand reuses one collective
      Concept name.

      A component with recurring admission and publication concerns uses two
      Concepts while keeping its operation signature and shared guarantees direct.

      A small single-concern component keeps clear direct Facets without a wrapper
      that only repeats its component identity.

      A public concern can receive an interface Tag identity for consumer reuse
      without filler occurrences in the remaining contracts.

      An accessible imported public identity is reused instead of creating a synonym.

      Two accessible imported identities with the same name are reported for
      resolution rather than qualified with dotted syntax.
    }

DecisionRationaleWorkflow {
      An importer may reuse a provider's Tag introduced in `interface` in
      decisions to explain local rationale, while Scope confines that decision
      to the importer.

      A proposal that changes validation and enrichment ordering includes a matching
      decision record explaining why the order was selected.

      A proposal with no material selected choice reports the inspected changes and
      why no decision record is required.

      A written material constraint without matching durable rationale returns to
      proposal review before implementation.
    }
  }
}
